    {
      "text": "On the asymptotic expansion of various quantum invariants III: the Reshetikhin-Turaev invariants of closed hyperbolic 3-manifolds obtained by integral surgery along the figure-eight knot — This is\n\n**On the asymptotic expansion of various quantum invariants III: the Reshetikhin-Turaev invariants of closed hyperbolic 3-manifolds obtained by integral surgery along the figure-eight knot**\n\n62 pp, 19 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** This is the third article in a series devoted to the study of the asymptotic expansions of various quantum invariants related to the twist knots. In this paper, by us- ing the saddle point method developed by Ohtsuki and Yokota, we obtain an asymptotic expansion formula for the Reshetikhin-Turaev invariants of closed hyperbolic 3-manifolds obtained by doing integral q-surgery along the twist knotsKp at the root of unity e 4π√−1 r (r is odd).\n\n**Outline.** 1 Introduction; 2 Preliminaries; 2.1 Defintion of the Reshetikhin-Turaev invari; 2.2 Dilogarithm and Lobachevsky functions; 2.3 Quantum dilogrithm functions; 2.4 Saddle point method; 3 Computations of the potential function; 4 Poisson summation formula; 5 Asymptotic expansions; 5.1 Preparations; 5.5 Final proof; 6 Appendices; 6.1 Geometry of the critical point; 6.2 Critical value gives the complex volume; 6.3 Proof of Proposition 5.2; 6.4 Estimation of the critical value; 6.5 Two-dimensional saddle point method; 6.6 One-dimensional saddle point method\n\n**Extracted claims (proposals, not verified).**\n- Theorem 1.2: For (p,q )∈S, the asymptotic expansion of Reshetikhin-TuraevRTr(Mp,q)\n- Theorem 1.2: The final Appendix Section 6 is devoted to the proof of several results\n- Theorem 5.7: When m1 = 0 and m3≥ 1, then\n- Theorem 6.11: Moreover, when m3≥ 1, from the inequalities (6) and (7), we obtain\n- Theorem 5.8: When m1≥ 1 and m3 = 0, then\n- Theorem 6.12: Moreover, when m1≥ 1, from the inequalities (14), we obtain",
